---
description: Align columns whenever a list or table shows repeated records
alwaysApply: true
---

When a list or table shows repeated records — session rows, command menus, and any row with more than one field — put each field in its own column so the values line up.

- Measure width in terminal cells. CJK and other wide characters count as 2, not as `string.length`.
- Size each column from the whole list, not from a single row, so scrolling does not move the columns.
- Pad shorter cells with spaces. Clip an overflowing text cell with an ellipsis.
- Keep the identifying column readable, and clip secondary text first.
- Do not append a variable-length field and then a separator. The next field would start at a different column on each row.
